Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.22,0:00:03.49,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,You've been summoned\Nby an investigative committee?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.49,0:00:04.90,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.90,0:00:06.98,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Deborah Darkian, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.98,0:00:12.54,Flashback,Deborah,0,0,0,,I summon you to the Starlight Room \Nat the Grand Merillian for investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.77,0:00:18.81,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,This isn't legally enforceable. \NI don't see why you should play along.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.42,0:00:23.96,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I take it you're going?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.70,0:00:29.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm certain there's much more\N I need to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.60,0:00:35.98,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Do you know what they call \NDeborah's investigative committee?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.86,0:00:40.96,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Their gatherings are famous, \Nbut no one knows what transpires there.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.71,0:00:43.73,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,No one will breathe a word.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.88,0:00:46.72,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So it has acquired the name...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.97,0:00:52.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,the Silent Ladies' Tea Party.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.29,0:00:56.02,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Welcome, Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.57,0:00:59.61,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I see your head is still attached.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.35,0:02:34.71,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,While I assume you're aware,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.71,0:02:37.43,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,you are not to speak of anything\N that happens here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.17,0:02:40.51,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Do you still wish to proceed?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.06,0:02:42.32,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That won't be a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.95,0:02:46.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,These three are Deborah's hangers-on.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.92,0:02:53.52,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,The thing is, I received a letter \Nfrom your friend, Pamela Francis.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.82,0:02:55.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,From Pamela?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.37,0:03:00.37,Default,Esther,0,0,0,,The poor dear. I hear her hair \Nhas turned white as snow.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.83,0:03:05.86,Default,Janine,0,0,0,,But she wrote saying that \Nnothing you did broke the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.86,0:03:10.62,Default,Caroline,0,0,0,,So you see, someone else \Nmust step in to review your crimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.97,0:03:12.50,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,{\i1}My{\i0} crimes?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.75,0:03:17.00,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,We mean to say we'll do you \Nthe honor of judging you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.31,0:03:21.76,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,You wouldn't want to end up like \NScarlett Castiel, now would you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.11,0:03:23.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.06,0:03:27.27,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,It was simply dreadful.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.56,0:03:32.76,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,That face she was so proud of,\Nrolling through the mud like some toy...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.76,0:03:39.78,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Everyone—yes, even the most lowly—\Nclapped and laughed and jeered.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.28,0:03:47.29,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I know {\i1}I{\i0} could never bear the shame \Nof such an ignominious end.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.51,0:04:03.04,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What do you think you're doing?\N Holding my hand?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.60,0:04:10.30,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Up till now, we've switched \Nso she could save me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.97,0:04:13.05,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,But not this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.78,0:04:14.81,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,We're going...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.27,0:04:16.71,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,to fight together!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.84,0:04:21.56,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,This is a tawdry farce,\N but I'll play along.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.92,0:04:23.45,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I beg your pardon?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.45,0:04:25.96,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Didn't you hear me? Listen well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.96,0:04:27.07,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I said that I...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.53,0:04:32.33,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,that {\i1}we{\i0} are going to judge {\i1}you{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.17,0:04:36.20,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.61,0:04:41.08,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,The Earl John Doe Ball must have been \Nquite a blow to you, Deborah Darkian.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.59,0:04:43.84,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,You speak of the dancing children?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.84,0:04:47.75,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,With all due respect, it was I \Nwho reported them to the Security Force.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.75,0:04:50.34,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,To think we had human \Ntraffickers in our midst!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.11,0:04:53.84,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,The mere thought makes my blood run cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.42,0:04:59.28,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,And why did everyone there \Nhave ties to the Darkians, I wonder?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.12,0:05:04.87,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Take the Marquess of McLain, \Nwho looked so friendly with the slavers.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.22,0:05:06.34,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Esther,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.34,0:05:07.90,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I mean your husband.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.36,0:05:11.52,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I doubt he'll be able to avoid prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.52,0:05:12.36,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Then again,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.66,0:05:17.56,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,he may receive a lighter sentence \Nif he were to name the ringleader.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.41,0:05:21.63,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Surely you know of my fiancé's position.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.05,0:05:25.94,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,Depending on your testimony, I would \Nbe happy to put in a good word with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.73,0:05:31.89,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.54,0:05:34.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,We've as good as won.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.69,0:05:36.14,Default,Connie-S,0,0,0,,I leave the rest to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.40,0:05:38.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank you, Scarlett.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.87,0:05:49.40,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,The Marchioness of McLain must know \NDeborah Darkian had a hand in the crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.96,0:05:51.90,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,If I can get her to attest to that...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.90,0:05:53.15,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Ladies.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.27,0:05:57.87,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Did you hear something just now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.37,0:06:00.92,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Oh, that reminds me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.92,0:06:06.69,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Wasn't the Marquess of McLain \Njust about to leave the country?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.69,0:06:08.51,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Am I wrong, Esther?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.84,0:06:13.68,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,He won't be back for some time, will he?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.50,0:06:16.94,Default,Esther,0,0,0,,Th-That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.73,0:06:22.10,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.10,0:06:24.18,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,You still don't see?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.49,0:06:29.95,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Did you seriously imagine a viscount's \Ndaughter could crush a Darkian?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.76,0:06:36.47,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Now, I think it's time we took a vote.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.47,0:06:40.21,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Who should be judged here, you or me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.67,0:06:43.46,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,This isn't good.\NUnder the circumstances...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.71,0:06:48.99,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Of course, if you bend the knee \Nto me like a good little girl,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.99,0:06:52.46,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I might decide Pamela \Nwas only imagining things.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.46,0:06:54.23,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,How dare she?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.82,0:06:58.62,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Now, have you anything \Nto say for yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.62,0:07:00.70,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.70,0:07:01.98,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.43,0:07:03.86,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.46,0:07:08.36,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,don't agree with your methods one jot!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.40,0:07:13.30,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,They can do what they will with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.30,0:07:15.25,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I refuse to back down now!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.89,0:07:18.99,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,You little—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.09,0:07:23.26,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Why, hello there! Do pardon the intrusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.70,0:07:26.50,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Honestly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.50,0:07:30.51,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,They kept pestering me about formalities,\Nand now look how late it's gotten!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.82,0:07:36.74,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,How rude of you to barge in uninvited,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.74,0:07:38.52,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Abigail O'Brian.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.55,0:07:44.15,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,The four great noble families\N of our kingdom are the Castiels,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.15,0:07:47.41,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,the Richelieus, the Darkians, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.41,0:07:51.07,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,How do you do, young lady?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.07,0:07:52.03,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,This woman...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.52,0:07:53.84,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,She's an O'Brian!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.43,0:07:56.22,Default,Janine,0,0,0,,Um, that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.22,0:08:00.28,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Susannah Neville's seat, yes. \NI'm here in her place.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.28,0:08:01.86,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Here. My credentials.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.40,0:08:04.31,Default,Caroline,0,0,0,,Th-Then, if you'd sign here...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.31,0:08:06.60,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I have only one thing to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.44,0:08:12.68,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Esther. Janine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.68,0:08:14.17,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Caroline.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.81,0:08:17.92,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Unless you want to be crushed, \Ndo as I say.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.62,0:08:24.40,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Really, Abigail.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.40,0:08:26.80,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,That sounded like a threat.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.80,0:08:31.91,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,If you insist on menacing my friends,\NI must have legal recourse.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.22,0:08:35.02,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,We can't have that, Debbie.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.71,0:08:38.76,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Nothing said here leaves this room.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.25,0:08:41.15,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,You made that rule yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.57,0:08:47.92,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Forgive me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.37,0:08:52.23,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I don't feel at all well. \NYou must excuse me early today.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.67,0:08:59.17,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Really, dear, you mustn't \Ntake such thoughtless risks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.17,0:09:01.68,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,No quarter is given in our world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.14,0:09:05.41,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Um... Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.41,0:09:08.49,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,You'd best save your thanks \Nfor Randolph Ulster.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.49,0:09:10.70,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Why His Lordship?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.12,0:09:16.09,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Yesterday, he came calling at my house \Nand asked me to help his fiancée
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.09,0:09:18.69,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,because she seemed likely \Nto poke her nose into trouble.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.13,0:09:23.70,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,He'd looked into the participants here\Nand acquired this letter for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.54,0:09:29.20,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Why do I feel so, I don't know...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.32,0:09:31.80,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,warm and fuzzy?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.96,0:09:41.46,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Constance Grail?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.98,0:09:44.23,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,I knew it!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.78,0:09:47.92,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Say, could you spare me a few words?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.92,0:09:49.70,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Er, um, who might you—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.70,0:09:53.42,Main - Top,Amelia,0,0,0,,When did you start looking up\N to Scarlett Castiel?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.23,0:09:58.86,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Are you rebelling against the famous\N Grail family ideal of sincerity?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.86,0:10:00.75,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Did you tire of being a good girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.04,0:10:05.75,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Must've been frustrating when the papers\Nall focused on Teresa Jennings's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.75,0:10:08.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Huh? Wh-Who's Teresa?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.59,0:10:13.11,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You don't remember? She was half \Nof that scene at Emilia's ball.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.55,0:10:17.97,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, her!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.48,0:10:21.11,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Why, didn't you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.11,0:10:23.41,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,The man she was having\Nan affair with broke it off,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.41,0:10:26.41,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,and she tried to kill him\Nwhen she took her own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.35,0:10:29.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You mean she's...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.69,0:10:33.63,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,But enough about that! How do you \Nand your fiancé, Randolph Ulster—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.01,0:10:35.02,Main - Top,Aldous,0,0,0,,Don't you think that's enough, Amelia?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.01,0:10:39.36,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,Aldous!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.59,0:10:45.65,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,The editor in chief said he'd demote you \Nif you do any more unscheduled interviews.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.76,0:10:47.20,Main - Top,Amelia,0,0,0,,Until next time, Constance Grail!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.20,0:10:50.44,Default,Amelia,0,0,0,,I have every faith \Nyou'll answer sincerely, of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.90,0:10:53.86,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So she's a reporter?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.86,0:10:55.37,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Good grief.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.37,0:10:57.28,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Please forgive me colleague.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.28,0:10:58.64,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, no need.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.88,0:11:02.14,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,I'm Aldous Clayton, \Nwith the Mayflower Company.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.14,0:11:06.14,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Do let me know if Amelia \Ncauses you any more bother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.52,0:11:08.06,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.72,0:11:13.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What was that about?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.69,0:11:17.01,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Just think of her as a cat \Nthat happened to scratch at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.76,0:11:24.00,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,"Miss C., the daughter of a viscount,\Nemulates the infamous Scarlett Castiel."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.00,0:11:29.50,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,"She indulges in now-banned hallucinogens\Nand spends her days in wild orgies."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.79,0:11:33.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It's nonsense! Awful hogwash!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.79,0:11:35.50,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Well, of course it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.50,0:11:40.29,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,What a shame. And here I was, looking up\N to Amelia Hobbes as a role model.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.29,0:11:42.52,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,A role model? Her?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.52,0:11:44.05,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Didn't I tell you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.05,0:11:47.52,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,My dream is to stay unmarried\N and become a reporter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.83,0:11:49.51,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Is it really?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.09,0:11:53.03,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,You told me yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.47,0:11:56.62,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,I've always been obsessed \Nwith chasing rumors,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.62,0:12:00.00,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,so you said, "If you enjoy it so, \Nwhy not become a reporter?"
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.00,0:12:03.41,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,No one else would suggest such a thing \Nto me at the time, even as a joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.96,0:12:07.20,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,It felt like you truly saw me. \NI was delighted.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.95,0:12:09.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.02,0:12:14.50,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,Now, you're having tea with \NCrown Princess Cecilia later, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.50,0:12:16.53,Default,Mylene,0,0,0,,I expect a juicy scoop!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.89,0:12:19.30,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, right...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.58,0:12:24.80,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,May I have a moment of your time?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.54,0:12:28.54,Main - Top,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I represent the Ladies' Committee \Nof the Violet Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.54,0:12:30.81,Main - Top,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Kimberly Smith is my name.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.58,0:12:33.32,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What now?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.57,0:12:39.57,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,We are working to rid our land \Nof inhumane culture.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.57,0:12:45.82,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I've come to remonstrate with the foolish \Nyoung lady who idolizes Scarlett Castiel.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.14,0:12:47.70,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,I want to leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.95,0:12:50.43,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,This bit about hallucinogens \Nin particular.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.43,0:12:54.70,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Don't tell me it's referring \Nto Jackal's Paradise.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.20,0:12:56.97,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Jackal's Paradise?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.54,0:12:59.71,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Speaking of Jackal's Paradise...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.71,0:13:01.74,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Where do you think you're looking?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.25,0:13:04.62,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,You don't want the likes \Nof me in your sight?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.62,0:13:06.05,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,How very aristocratic.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.05,0:13:10.14,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,You bigots don't even consider \Nus common folk human.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.14,0:13:11.97,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I d-don't think that's fair to—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.72,0:13:15.97,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Are my parents bigots too, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.58,0:13:17.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.94,0:13:19.72,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,Aren't you the Lorraines' daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.31,0:13:24.87,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I come from a baronial family, \Nbut my mother was born a commoner.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.87,0:13:28.73,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Are we still bigots simply \Nbecause we're of the nobility?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.48,0:13:35.24,Default,Kimberly,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you must excuse me for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.56,0:13:39.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate, thank y—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.13,0:13:41.57,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,Is it true you got engaged \Nto the Earl of Ulster?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.26,0:13:43.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.33,0:13:46.69,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,So it is true.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.89,0:13:49.90,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,You won't tell me anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.36,0:13:53.27,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,I know I said I'd wait for you to open up,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.59,0:13:57.02,Default,Kate,0,0,0,,but that doesn't mean this doesn't hurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.25,0:13:58.35,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kate...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.91,0:14:07.40,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What do I do now?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.63,0:14:11.40,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How could I have been so awful to Kate?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.87,0:14:16.69,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,Still, I can't drag her into this. \NNot Kate, of all people.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.24,0:14:20.49,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Miss Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.92,0:14:22.17,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.74,0:14:26.51,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,U-Um, thank you so much\N for the other day.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.80,0:14:28.26,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What for?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.17,0:14:32.01,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,For the investigative committee.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.79,0:14:35.77,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I see. She didn't mince words.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.06,0:14:37.96,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,How like Abigail.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.26,0:14:41.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Yes. I'll have to pay her \Na thank-you visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.84,0:14:49.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What could be the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.78,0:14:52.78,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That's Kendall Levine, \Na high-ranking diplomat.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.11,0:14:55.60,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,He's a special envoy from Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.60,0:14:57.43,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What could have him so flustered?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.17,0:15:02.01,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It sounds like they've lost \Na member of their delegation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.14,0:15:04.32,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Is Scarlett there?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.32,0:15:06.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes. You see...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.54,0:15:09.83,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Ulysses?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.83,0:15:13.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Someone by that name \Nhas been missing since yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.54,0:15:14.93,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Do you know him?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.93,0:15:21.14,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That's probably Ulysses Faris, \Nthe nine-year-old seventh prince of Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.14,0:15:22.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A p-prince?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.94,0:15:24.54,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,A kidnapping, perhaps?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.54,0:15:25.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How horrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.00,0:15:29.62,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,In that case, why haven't\N the Farisians said anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.18,0:15:32.57,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Pardon me, Miss Grail. I must—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.57,0:15:35.06,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Return to the Security Force, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.39,0:15:39.45,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Prince Ulysses is bound \Nto be terribly anxious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.45,0:15:41.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Please find him as soon \Nas you possibly can.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.58,0:15:45.30,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I will. As for your meeting \Nwith Crown Princess Cecilia...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.30,0:15:46.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.92,0:15:49.46,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Her Royal Highness won't \Ntrip me up if I can help it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.46,0:15:51.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,If all else fails,\N I'll use Your Lordship's name.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.71,0:15:56.32,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I may be no match for her \Neven then, but nevertheless...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.23,0:16:03.45,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Well said.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.60,0:16:07.10,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,In any case...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.10,0:16:11.51,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'm intrigued by who could possibly\Nabduct someone amid all this security.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.51,0:16:13.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your intuition again?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.65,0:16:17.12,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We still have time. \NI'll see what I can find.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.12,0:16:22.27,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Welcome!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.27,0:16:24.12,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Why, where's Randy?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.33,0:16:28.64,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry. \NUrgent business called him away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.62,0:16:31.31,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Too bad for him!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.31,0:16:32.84,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Now, have a seat! Have a seat!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.84,0:16:35.63,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I haven't had a guest \Nin this room in ages!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.22,0:16:38.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Did you learn anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.59,0:16:40.78,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I discovered one suspicious man.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.78,0:16:43.51,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Vado, a merchant \Nfrom the Republic of Soldita.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.29,0:16:46.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,He came to see Cecilia.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.25,0:16:53.11,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Unusual, aren't they?\NThey came from all over the continent.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.50,0:16:55.49,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I have a merchant who finds them for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.49,0:16:57.43,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,He's ever so good at his job.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.28,0:17:04.11,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Does this merchant... call on you often?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.11,0:17:06.83,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Yes. His name's Vado, by the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.83,0:17:08.28,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,He was here just yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.28,0:17:12.29,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,He came with a massive wicker hamper\Non his back full of carpets to sell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.76,0:17:15.06,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,But why do you ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.06,0:17:16.43,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,N-No reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.43,0:17:17.54,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Oh, I'm so sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.79,0:17:19.04,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,The tea will get cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.33,0:17:24.06,Main - Italics,Connie,0,0,0,,What a distinctive smell.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.53,0:17:27.95,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Oh, yours is ordinary black tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.38,0:17:33.22,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I used to be rather sickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.22,0:17:37.58,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Vado fetches me \Nthis special herbal tea as a favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.02,0:17:40.47,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, that's why we have separate pots?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.47,0:17:42.58,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Of course. Why else?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.95,0:17:44.69,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'm terribly sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.69,0:17:48.57,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The attempted poisoning of \NYour Royal Highness is so famous,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.57,0:17:51.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I assumed you must \Nalways be on your guard.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.08,0:17:54.13,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,You mean Scarlett Castiel?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.51,0:17:56.60,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,You speak as though \Nyou know all about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.60,0:17:59.08,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No, I've only heard rumors.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.51,0:18:02.10,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Then I'll tell you the story.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.11,0:18:03.98,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,That day,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.34,0:18:07.23,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Enrique reneged on\N an appointment with Scarlett
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.23,0:18:09.69,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,in order to pay me a get-well visit.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.59,0:18:13.38,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,She was furious.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.42,0:18:21.14,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,That very night, we found that one \Nof our water jars had been poisoned.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.90,0:18:26.24,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Her earring lay beside the poisoned jar,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.24,0:18:30.30,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,and a half-empty bottle of poison \Nwas discovered in her home.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.73,0:18:34.20,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,The rest happened just as you've heard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.20,0:18:37.12,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,She was executed for her crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.59,0:18:44.89,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,But I am guilty of falling in love\N with Enrique when I knew he was engaged.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.67,0:18:52.21,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,And it's my fault that he has \Nno children. Poor Enrique.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.96,0:18:57.27,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I think he means to cede the throne \Nto Johan, his younger brother,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.27,0:18:59.54,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,who has a son and a daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.52,0:19:01.87,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Royal Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.87,0:19:06.21,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Her woe-is-me act doesn't seem to have \Nwon her any favor around here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.43,0:19:12.16,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Take that herbal tea. It has poison\N meant to terminate pregnancy.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.49,0:19:16.43,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,If she's always drinking it, \Nit'd wreak havoc on her insides.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.92,0:19:20.28,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Her body must be as cold as ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.54,0:19:27.01,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.01,0:19:29.30,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, nothing! Just...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.77,0:19:33.16,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The thing is...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.77,0:19:36.28,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,How stupid can you be?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.28,0:19:40.72,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Leave well enough alone. \NNow you've made yourself a target.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.72,0:19:45.28,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But I couldn't just let \Nan unsuspecting person drink poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.66,0:19:49.41,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Oh? Did you ever consider\N I might be making it up?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.41,0:19:52.00,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You may be a liar, Scarlett,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.01,0:19:56.76,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,but I can still tell \Nwhen you're speaking the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.81,0:20:03.42,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You've certainly gotten \Ncheeky lately, girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.99,0:20:08.30,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Now, about that merchant... \NShe said he was carrying a hamper.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.30,0:20:09.17,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.48,0:20:12.26,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You could hide a small child in that.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.26,0:20:14.19,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,We'd better do a bit more digging.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.45,0:20:15.60,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.99,0:20:17.94,Main - Top,Scarlett,0,0,0,,To learn of a professional,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.51,0:20:20.90,Main - Top,Scarlett,0,0,0,,ask someone in the same trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.72,0:20:37.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,After all that,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.44,0:20:42.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,we've learned Faris has a monopoly \Non that abortion drug,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.21,0:20:46.34,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,but no one knows this man named Vado.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.34,0:20:51.23,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,My, my. No one knows a man \Nimportant enough to visit the palace?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.23,0:20:54.56,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,That sounds like extremely valuable \Ninformation, if you ask me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.88,0:20:56.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Do you really think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.92,0:21:01.64,Default,Coachman A,0,0,0,,So sorry. Something seems \Nto be wrong with the rear wheels.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.64,0:21:03.27,Default,Coachman A,0,0,0,,I'll just be checking on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.27,0:21:04.45,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,C-Certainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.79,0:21:09.40,Default,Coachman B,0,0,0,,Please pardon the delay.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.40,0:21:12.12,Default,Coachman B,0,0,0,,As I feared, one of the rear wheels \Nis about to fall off.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.12,0:21:13.21,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.50,0:21:16.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.75,0:21:18.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,He sounded... different.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.68,0:21:22.97,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,The coachman's voice is different \Nfrom when we got in.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.26,0:21:36.23,Default,Coachman B,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.21,0:21:40.52,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Why was the driver replaced?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.52,0:21:42.35,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Could this man be...?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.34,0:21:45.75,Flashback,Connie,0,0,0,,A {\i1}spell{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.75,0:21:48.64,Flashback,Tony,0,0,0,,Yeah. For spotting bad guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.15,0:21:53.63,Flashback,Lily,0,0,0,,If they react to it at all, \Nyou'll know they're very bad people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.74,0:21:57.70,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Kiriki kirikuku.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.56,0:22:04.47,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Stand aside!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.22,0:22:16.27,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.98,0:22:22.06,Signs,Signs; title,0,0,0,,THE SILENT LADIES' TEA PARTY
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.07,0:22:28.12,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(480,524)\fs12\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(181.286,315.714)}Translation:\h\h\h\h\h\h\hWilliam Varteresian
